/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `tasks` DISABLE KEYS */;
INSERT INTO `tasks` VALUES (1,1,'Environment Setup','You have just joined the backend team at \"ShopMega\". Your first task is to get the development environment running on your machine so you can start contributing to the codebase. You should initialize a new Laravel project using Composer. Then, configure your local development environment (using Laravel Sail, Docker, or XAMPP) and update the .env file to establish a connection to your local MySQL database. Finally, verify the setup by running the default migrations.',NULL,NULL,'A fresh Laravel installation should be accessible at http://localhost, displaying the default Laravel welcome page. The .env file must be configured with valid database credentials (DB_HOST, DB_DATABASE, DB_USERNAME, DB_PASSWORD). Running `php artisan migrate` should execute successfully, creating the default `users`, `password_reset_tokens`, `failed_jobs`, and `personal_access_tokens` tables in your MySQL database.','DevOps','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(2,1,'Database Migration','The lead architect has handed you the ER diagram for the core system. You need to translate this into Laravel migrations to set up the database structure. You should design and create database migrations for the core entities: Products (with columns for name, price, stock), Orders (with columns for user_id, total, status), and Users (with columns for name, email, password). Ensure you use appropriate data types (e.g., decimal for price, integer for stock) and add indexing for performance where necessary.',NULL,NULL,'The database must contain `products`, `orders`, and `users` tables. The `products` table should have `id`, `name` (string), `price` (decimal), `stock` (integer), and timestamps. The `orders` table should have `id`, `user_id` (foreign key), `total` (decimal), `status` (string), and timestamps. The `users` table should have `id`, `name`, `email` (unique), `password`, and timestamps. Verify the schema using a database client like phpMyAdmin, TablePlus, or DBeaver.','Database','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(3,1,'Basic Product API','The frontend team is waiting for the Product API to start building the catalog page. You need to provide them with endpoints to fetch and create products. You should develop a RESTful API controller for Products. Implement endpoints for listing all products (GET /api/products), showing a single product (GET /api/products/{id}), and creating a product (POST /api/products). You should use Laravel Resources to format the JSON response consistently.',NULL,NULL,'A GET request to `/api/products` should return a JSON array of product objects, each containing `id`, `name`, `price`, and `stock`. A GET request to `/api/products/{id}` should return the details of a specific product. A POST request to `/api/products` with a JSON body containing `name`, `price`, and `stock` should create a new record in the `products` table and return the created product with a 201 Created status code.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(4,1,'Shopping Cart Service','To improve performance, we decided to store shopping carts in Redis instead of the database. You are responsible for implementing this high-speed cart service. You should implement a temporary shopping cart system using Redis. Create API endpoints to add items to a cart, remove items from a cart, and view the current cart contents. Ensure the cart data expires automatically after a set duration (e.g., 24 hours).',NULL,NULL,'Redis should store cart data using a key pattern like `cart:{userId}`. A POST request to `/api/cart` with `productId` and `quantity` should update the Redis hash. A GET request to `/api/cart` should return the list of items in the cart. The Redis key should have a TTL (Time To Live) set.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(5,1,'Payment Gateway Integration','We need to process payments. Since we are in dev mode, integrate a mock provider, but structure the code so we can easily swap it for Stripe later. You should integrate a mock payment gateway service (or use Stripe Test mode). Create a dedicated service class that handles the payment processing logic and returns a standardized success or failure response. You must ensure all payment attempts are logged for auditing purposes.',NULL,NULL,'The payment API endpoint should return a 200 OK status with a mock transaction ID (e.g., `txn_12345`) upon successful payment. The `storage/logs/laravel.log` file should contain an entry like \"Payment processed for Order #123: Success\".','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(6,1,'Email Notification Service','Users are complaining they don\'t get confirmation emails instantly. Move the email sending logic to a background queue to prevent blocking the checkout response. You should set up a Laravel Queue worker to handle background jobs. Create a Job class (e.g., `SendOrderConfirmation`) that sends an order confirmation email to the user after a successful checkout. Configure the queue driver in `.env` to use Redis or Database.',NULL,NULL,'After placing an order, a new job should appear in the `jobs` table (if using database driver) or Redis queue. Running `php artisan queue:work` in the terminal should process the job, and the log should indicate \"Processed: App\\Jobs\\SendOrderConfirmation\".','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(7,1,'User Authentication','Security audit revealed that anyone can place orders! Secure the API so that only logged-in users can access sensitive endpoints. Implement secure API authentication using Laravel Sanctum or JWT. Protect the order placement and user profile endpoints so only authenticated users can access them. Implement login and registration controllers.',NULL,NULL,'Requests to protected endpoints without a valid Bearer token return 401 Unauthorized. Successful login returns a valid token.','Security','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(8,1,'Product Catalog Service','The product list page is loading too slowly during high traffic. Implement caching to reduce the load on the database. Refactor the Product API into a dedicated service. Implement caching using Redis to store the product list for faster retrieval. Ensure the cache is invalidated or updated when a product is modified.',NULL,NULL,'First request hits the DB, subsequent requests hit Redis (check Redis keys). Updating a product clears the cache.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(9,1,'Admin Dashboard API','The operations team needs a way to manage inventory. Build an Admin API, but make sure regular users can\'t access it. Create a set of administrative API endpoints for managing products and orders. Implement Middleware to ensure only users with an \"admin\" role can access these routes.',NULL,NULL,'Accessing `/api/admin/*` as a normal user returns 403 Forbidden. Admin users can access CRUD operations.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(10,1,'Search Service','Users are having trouble finding products. Implement a robust search engine to improve product discoverability. Implement full-text search capabilities for the product catalog. Use Laravel Scout with a driver like Meilisearch or Algolia (or a basic database driver) to allow users to search products by name or description.',NULL,NULL,'Searching for \"Laptop\" returns relevant product results quickly, even with a large dataset.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(11,1,'Inventory Management','We oversold the \"Super Widget\" yesterday because two people bought the last one at the exact same second. Fix this race condition. Implement logic to handle stock deduction when an order is placed. Use database transactions and locking (pessimistic or optimistic) to prevent race conditions where two users buy the last item simultaneously.',NULL,NULL,'Simultaneous requests for the last item result in only one successful order. Stock count never goes below zero.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(12,1,'API Gateway Implementation','We are splitting the monolith into microservices. Set up a Gateway so the frontend only needs to talk to one URL. Set up a simple API Gateway (using a proxy or a dedicated tool like Kong or a Laravel wrapper) that routes incoming requests to the appropriate microservices (Product Service, Order Service, Auth Service).',NULL,NULL,'All requests go through a single port (e.g., 8000) and are correctly routed to backend services (e.g., 8001, 8002).','DevOps','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(13,1,'Service Architecture Design','Before we scale further, we need a blueprint. Document the architecture and API contracts for the new microservices system. Draft a comprehensive architecture document detailing how the microservices communicate. Define the API contracts (using OpenAPI/Swagger) and choose a communication protocol (REST vs gRPC).',NULL,NULL,'A `docker-compose.yml` file defining all services and a `swagger.yaml` file documenting the API endpoints.','System Design','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(14,1,'Order Management Service','The Order service is too tightly coupled. Extract it and make it react to payment events asynchronously. Decouple the Order logic into its own microservice. Use an event-driven approach where the Order Service listens for \"PaymentSuccessful\" events via Kafka or RabbitMQ to trigger order creation.',NULL,NULL,'Publishing a message to the \"payments\" topic triggers the Order Service to create a new order record.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(15,1,'Centralized Logging','Debugging across 5 services is a nightmare. Centralize the logs so we can trace a request across the entire system. Implement a centralized logging strategy. Configure all microservices to ship their logs to an ELK (Elasticsearch, Logstash, Kibana) stack or a similar solution to view logs in one place.',NULL,NULL,'Logs from all containers are visible in the Kibana dashboard, searchable by service name.','DevOps','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(16,1,'Monitoring & Metrics','Instrument your applications to expose metrics (CPU, memory, request count). Set up Prometheus to scrape these metrics and Grafana to visualize them in a dashboard.','We had downtime yesterday and didn\'t know until customers complained. Set up monitoring to alert us of issues.',NULL,'A Grafana dashboard showing real-time graphs of request latency and error rates.','DevOps','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(17,1,'CI/CD Pipeline Setup','Create a CI/CD pipeline using GitHub Actions or GitLab CI. The pipeline should automatically run unit tests (PHPUnit) and style checks whenever code is pushed to the repository.','Manual deployments are causing errors. Automate the testing and deployment process.',NULL,'Pushing code triggers a GitHub Action workflow that passes (green checkmark) only if tests pass.','DevOps','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(18,1,'Load Testing & Optimization','Perform load testing using tools like JMeter or k6. Simulate high traffic to the API Gateway and identify bottlenecks. Optimize database queries and cache configurations based on the results.','Black Friday is coming. Stress test the system to ensure it can handle the expected traffic spike.',NULL,'A report showing the max requests per second (RPS) the system can handle before and after optimization.','DevOps','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(19,2,'Frontend Setup','You are the lead frontend dev for a new startup \"ChatGenius\". Your first milestone is to get the React boilerplate up and running. You should initialize a new React application using Create React App or Vite. Then, set up the basic folder structure and install necessary dependencies like React Router for navigation and a CSS framework (e.g., Tailwind CSS or Material UI) for styling.',NULL,NULL,'A React application should be running on http://localhost:3000 (or 5173 for Vite). The browser console should be free of errors. The main page should render a \"Welcome to Chat\" header styled with the chosen CSS framework.','Frontend','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(20,2,'Static Chat UI','Before we connect to the backend, we need a visual prototype. Build the chat UI so we can show it to investors. You should design and build the chat interface components: a Sidebar for channels/users, a Chat Window for the conversation, and a Message Input area. Use mock data to populate the interface. Ensure the layout is responsive and the message list scrolls correctly when new messages are added.',NULL,NULL,'A responsive chat interface should be visible. The sidebar should list mock channels. The main area should display mock messages with distinct styles for sent (right-aligned) and received (left-aligned) messages. The message list should automatically scroll to the bottom.','Frontend','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(21,2,'Node.js API','The backend team is swamped. You need to spin up a simple Node.js server to handle user authentication. You should create a basic backend API using Express.js or NestJS. Implement a POST `/login` endpoint that accepts a username and password, validates them, and returns a JWT token. Set up a simple in-memory array or a database (like MongoDB) to store user credentials.',NULL,NULL,'A Node.js server should be running on port 5000. Sending a POST request to `http://localhost:5000/login` with valid JSON credentials should return a 200 OK response containing a JWT access token. Invalid credentials should return a 401 Unauthorized response.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(22,2,'User Presence','Users want to know who is online. Implement a real-time presence feature using WebSockets. You should implement real-time user presence using Socket.io. When a user connects to the socket server, broadcast their \"online\" status to all other connected clients. Update the frontend UI to display a green dot next to the names of online users.',NULL,NULL,'When a user opens the app in a second browser tab (simulating a second user), the first tab should immediately update to show the new user as \"Online\" with a visual indicator (e.g., green dot). Closing the second tab should trigger an \"Offline\" status update in the first tab.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(23,2,'Typing Indicators','It\'s annoying not knowing if someone is replying. Add a typing indicator to improve the UX. You should add a \"User is typing...\" feature. Emit a socket event (e.g., `typing`) when the user types in the input box, and listen for this event on other clients to display a visual typing indicator.',NULL,NULL,'When a user starts typing in one client, other clients in the same chat should see a \"User is typing...\" message or animation. The indicator should disappear automatically after a short delay (e.g., 2-3 seconds) once the user stops typing.','Frontend','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(24,2,'Message History Persistence','Chats are disappearing when we refresh the page! Persist the messages to a MongoDB database. You should connect the backend to a MongoDB database. Create a Mongoose schema for Messages (including sender, content, timestamp) and save every new chat message to the database. Create an API endpoint to fetch the chat history when the application loads.',NULL,NULL,'Refreshing the browser page should retrieve and display previous messages from the MongoDB database. The messages must appear in the correct chronological order. Check the MongoDB collection to verify that new messages are being inserted as documents.','Database','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(25,2,'Chat UI Component','The component state is getting messy. Refactor the chat logic to use Redux for better state management. Refactor the chat state management using Redux or Context API. Ensure that incoming socket messages update the global state and re-render the message list component efficiently.',NULL,NULL,'The Redux DevTools show actions being dispatched when messages arrive. The UI updates without a full page reload.','Frontend','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(26,2,'File Sharing Support','Users want to share memes. Add a file upload button to the chat input. Implement file upload functionality. Allow users to select an image or file, upload it to the server (or cloud storage), and send the file URL as a message attachment.',NULL,NULL,'Uploading an image displays it in the chat window. Clicking the image opens it in a new tab.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:41'),(27,2,'Group Channels','We need more than just one global chat. Implement \"Channels\" so teams can have separate conversations. Extend the data model to support Channels. Create API endpoints to create a channel, join a channel, and list available channels. Update the socket logic to broadcast messages only to users in the specific channel room.',NULL,NULL,'Messages sent in \"General\" channel do not appear in \"Random\" channel. Users can switch between channels via the sidebar.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:41','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(28,2,'Push Notifications','Users are missing messages when they are in other tabs. Add browser push notifications to alert them. Implement browser push notifications using the Web Push API or a library. Request permission from the user and trigger a notification when a new message arrives while the tab is in the background.',NULL,NULL,'Receiving a message while the tab is minimized triggers a system notification (toast) on the OS.','Frontend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(29,2,'Voice/Video Call Integration','Text is not enough. We need to compete with Zoom. Add a basic video calling feature using WebRTC. Integrate WebRTC to allow peer-to-peer voice or video calls. Implement the signaling logic using your existing WebSocket server to exchange SDP offers and answers.',NULL,NULL,'Two users can establish a video call. Local and remote video streams are visible.','Frontend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(30,2,'Message Encryption','Privacy is a major concern. Encrypt direct messages so even we (the admins) can\'t read them. Implement End-to-End encryption for private messages. Generate key pairs in the browser and encrypt the message payload before sending it to the server, so the server cannot read the content.',NULL,NULL,'Intercepting the network request shows encrypted gibberish in the payload. The recipient client successfully decrypts and displays the text.','Security','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(31,2,'WebSocket Server Setup','The monolithic server is struggling with 500 users. Extract the WebSocket logic into a dedicated microservice. Refactor the WebSocket server for scalability. Use a dedicated NestJS Gateway or a separate microservice for handling socket connections, ensuring it can handle thousands of concurrent users.',NULL,NULL,'The socket server runs as a standalone process. Connecting 1000 simulated clients works without crashing.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(32,2,'Message Queue Integration','Database writes are slowing down the chat. Use a message queue to handle persistence asynchronously. Decouple message processing using RabbitMQ. When a message is sent, publish it to a queue. Have a worker service consume the queue to persist the message to the database.',NULL,NULL,'Messages are delivered instantly to clients, but database writes happen asynchronously via the worker.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(33,2,'User Profile Management','Users want to customize their profiles. Allow them to upload avatars and set status messages. Create a user profile page where users can update their display name, avatar, and status message. Ensure these updates are reflected in real-time across all connected clients.',NULL,NULL,'Changing the avatar in one tab immediately updates the avatar icon in all other users\' chat views.','Frontend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(34,2,'Search Messages','I can\'t find that link someone sent last week. Add a search bar to the chat history. Implement a search feature for chat history. Use MongoDB text search or an external search engine to allow users to find past messages by keyword.',NULL,NULL,'Searching for a keyword returns a list of matching messages with timestamps.','Database','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(35,2,'Scalability: Redis Adapter','We are adding more servers. Configure Redis Adapter so users on Server A can talk to users on Server B. Configure the Socket.io Redis Adapter. This allows you to run multiple instances of your socket server and have them communicate, ensuring messages reach users connected to different server nodes.',NULL,NULL,'Users connected to Server Instance A can chat with users connected to Server Instance B.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(36,2,'Deployment to Kubernetes','It\'s time to go to production. Deploy the entire stack to a Kubernetes cluster. Containerize the application and deploy it to a Kubernetes cluster. Create deployment and service manifests, and set up an Ingress controller for external access.',NULL,NULL,'`kubectl get pods` shows running pods for frontend, backend, and database. The app is accessible via a public IP.','DevOps','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(37,3,'Project Structure','You are starting a new R&D project. Set up a clean Python environment so the team can collaborate without dependency hell. Set up the Python environment using venv or conda. Create a `requirements.txt` file with necessary libraries (FastAPI, uvicorn, opencv-python, tensorflow). Initialize a Git repository.',NULL,NULL,'A python virtual environment is active. Running `pip freeze` lists FastAPI, uvicorn, opencv-python, and tensorflow.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(38,3,'Basic Scripting','Verify that OpenCV is working correctly by writing a simple script to load and display an image. Write a Python script using OpenCV to read an image file from disk and display it in a window. This verifies that your image processing libraries are correctly installed.',NULL,NULL,'Running `python read_image.py` opens a window displaying the test image. The console prints the image dimensions (e.g., \"Image shape: (1920, 1080, 3)\").','AI/Data','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(39,3,'Image Preprocessing','Neural networks need consistent input. Write a preprocessing pipeline to resize and normalize images before training. Create a function to preprocess images for the model. This should include resizing the image to a fixed size (e.g., 224x224) and normalizing pixel values to be between 0 and 1.',NULL,NULL,'The script outputs a processed image array. The shape should be (224, 224, 3) and pixel values should be floats between 0.0 and 1.0.','AI/Data','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(40,3,'Simple API','We need to expose our model as a web service. Spin up a basic FastAPI server to get started. Create a basic FastAPI application with a single GET / endpoint that returns a JSON \"Hello World\" message. Run the server using Uvicorn to ensure it works.',NULL,NULL,'Visiting `http://localhost:8000/` in the browser displays `{\"message\": \"Hello World\"}`. The Swagger UI is accessible at `/docs`.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(41,3,'Data Augmentation Pipeline','We don\'t have enough training data. Use data augmentation to artificially increase the dataset size. Implement a data augmentation pipeline using TensorFlow or Keras. Generate new training samples by applying random rotations, flips, and zooms to your existing dataset.',NULL,NULL,'The script saves 5 new versions of the input image to an `augmented/` folder, each with different transformations (rotation, flip, zoom).','AI/Data','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(42,3,'Model Evaluation Metrics','Accuracy isn\'t everything. Implement a script to calculate Precision, Recall, and F1-score to better understand model performance. Write a script to calculate evaluation metrics. Given a set of true labels and predicted labels, compute the Accuracy, Precision, Recall, and F1-score.',NULL,NULL,'The script prints a classification report to the console showing Precision, Recall, and F1-score for each class, along with the overall accuracy.','AI/Data','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(43,3,'Model Training','It\'s time to train the brain. Build and train a CNN to classify images with at least 85% accuracy. Train a Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) on a standard dataset (like CIFAR-10 or MNIST). Save the trained model to an .h5 or .keras file once it achieves a satisfactory accuracy (>85%).',NULL,NULL,'A `model.h5` file is created. The training logs show validation accuracy exceeding 85%.','AI/Data','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(44,3,'Prediction API','Connect the brain to the web. Create an API endpoint that accepts an image and returns the model\'s prediction. Create a POST /predict endpoint in FastAPI. This endpoint should accept an image file upload, preprocess it using your function, run it through the trained model, and return the predicted class.',NULL,NULL,'Sending a POST request with an image of a cat returns `{\"class\": \"cat\", \"confidence\": 0.98}`.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(45,3,'Hyperparameter Tuning','The model is good, but can it be better? Tune the hyperparameters to squeeze out more accuracy. Experiment with different hyperparameters (learning rate, batch size, number of layers) to improve model performance. Log the results of each run to compare them.',NULL,NULL,'A CSV file or TensorBoard log containing comparison data of at least 3 different model configurations.','AI/Data','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(46,3,'Model Versioning','We need to A/B test models. Implement a versioning system so we can easily switch between model files. Implement a system to manage model versions. Allow the API to load a specific version of the model based on a configuration file or environment variable.',NULL,NULL,'Setting `MODEL_VERSION=v1` loads `model_v1.h5`. Changing it to `v2` loads `model_v2.h5` without code changes.','DevOps','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(47,3,'Batch Prediction Endpoint','Processing one image at a time is too slow for bulk uploads. Add a batch prediction endpoint. Add support for batch predictions. Create an endpoint that accepts a list of images (or a zip file) and returns predictions for all of them in a single response.',NULL,NULL,'Uploading a zip file with 10 images returns a JSON array with 10 prediction objects.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(48,3,'Frontend Image Upload UI','The backend is ready. Build a simple UI so non-technical users can try out the classifier. Build a simple React frontend that allows users to drag and drop an image. On drop, send the image to your FastAPI backend and display the returned prediction result.',NULL,NULL,'A web page with a drop zone. Dropping an image displays a loading spinner, then the prediction result text.','Frontend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(49,3,'Result Visualization','Enhance the frontend to visualize the model\'s confidence scores. Use a charting library (like Recharts or D3.js) to show a bar chart of probabilities for the top 5 classes.','Users want to know how sure the model is. Visualize the confidence scores for the top 5 predictions.',NULL,'The UI displays a bar chart where the X-axis is the class name and Y-axis is the probability.','Frontend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(50,3,'User Feedback Loop','Add a mechanism for users to correct the model. If the prediction is wrong, allow the user to submit the correct label, and save this data to a database for future retraining.','The model makes mistakes. Allow users to correct it so we can collect hard examples for retraining.',NULL,'Clicking \"Incorrect\" and selecting the right label saves a record in the `feedback` table with the image path and user correction.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(51,3,'Dockerize Model Service','Create a Dockerfile for the FastAPI application. Ensure it installs all dependencies and exposes the correct port. Build and run the container locally.','It works on your machine, but will it work on the server? Dockerize the application to ensure consistency.',NULL,'Running `docker run -p 8000:8000 my-model-service` makes the API accessible at localhost:8000.','DevOps','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(52,3,'GPU Acceleration Setup','Configure your training environment to use a GPU (if available) or Google Colab. Ensure TensorFlow is using the CUDA libraries for faster training.','Training is taking forever. Configure the environment to use GPU acceleration.',NULL,'`tf.config.list_physical_devices(\'GPU\')` returns a non-empty list. Training time is significantly reduced.','AI/Data','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(53,3,'API Rate Limiting','Implement rate limiting on your API using Redis or a middleware. Limit users to a certain number of prediction requests per minute to prevent abuse.','Someone is spamming our API! Implement rate limiting to protect our resources.',NULL,'Sending more than 60 requests in a minute results in a 429 Too Many Requests response.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(54,3,'Model Monitoring','Set up a monitoring script to track the distribution of predicted classes over time. Alert if the distribution shifts significantly (data drift).','Is the model still performing well in production? Set up monitoring to detect data drift.',NULL,'A dashboard or log file showing the percentage of predictions for each class over the last hour.','AI/Data','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(55,4,'UI Mockups','Design the app screens (Login, Dashboard, Workout Log, Profile) using Figma or Sketch. Then, convert these designs into HTML/CSS mockups or directly into React Native components to verify the layout.','You are the sole developer for \"FitTrack\". Start by designing the UI so you have a clear vision of what to build.',NULL,'A set of HTML files or React Native components that visually match the design. Navigation between the Login and Dashboard screens should work visually.','Frontend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(56,4,'App Navigation','Set up the navigation structure using React Navigation. Implement a Bottom Tab Navigator for the main sections and a Stack Navigator for drilling down into details (e.g., Workout Details).','Users need to move between screens. Implement a robust navigation system using React Navigation.',NULL,'Tapping the \"Workout\" tab switches the view to the Workout screen. The \"Back\" button in the stack navigator correctly returns to the previous screen.','Mobile','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(57,4,'User Authentication','Integrate Firebase Authentication. Allow users to sign up and log in using their email and password. Optionally, add Google Sign-In for easier access.','We need to know who is using the app. Integrate Firebase Auth to handle user accounts.',NULL,'Users can sign up with an email/password. The Firebase Console > Authentication tab shows the new user record. The app redirects to the Dashboard upon success.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(58,4,'Workout Logging','Create a form to log a workout session. Users should be able to add exercises, specify sets, reps, and weight. Store this data in Firestore under the user\'s ID.','The core feature is logging workouts. Build a form that saves exercise data to the cloud.',NULL,'Submitting the form adds a new document to the `workouts` collection in Firestore. The data includes the correct timestamp and exercise details.','Mobile','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(59,4,'Exercise Database','Populate a Firestore collection with a list of common exercises (e.g., Bench Press, Squat). Implement a search bar in the logging screen to allow users to find and select exercises.','Users shouldn\'t have to type \"Bench Press\" every time. Create a searchable database of exercises.',NULL,'Typing \"Bench\" in the search bar filters the list to show \"Bench Press\". Selecting it populates the exercise name field.','Database','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(60,4,'Progress Charts','Visualize the user\'s progress over time. Use a charting library (like react-native-chart-kit) to display a line graph of the max weight lifted for a specific exercise.','Users love seeing progress. Add a chart to show their strength gains over time.',NULL,'The chart correctly renders data points from Firestore. The X-axis shows dates and the Y-axis shows weight lifted.','Frontend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(61,4,'Profile Settings','Create a settings screen where users can update their profile information (height, weight) and preferences (units: kg/lbs). Save these preferences to Firestore.','Some users use kg, others use lbs. Allow them to configure their preferences in a settings screen.',NULL,'Changing the unit preference to \"lbs\" immediately updates the weight display on the Dashboard.','Frontend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(62,4,'Offline Support','Enable offline persistence in Firebase. Ensure that users can still view their history and log new workouts even when they don\'t have an internet connection, syncing when they reconnect.','Gyms often have bad Wi-Fi. Ensure the app works perfectly offline.',NULL,'Turning off Wi-Fi/Data and logging a workout still works. Reconnecting to the internet causes the new data to appear in the Firebase Console.','Mobile','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(63,4,'Social Sharing','Implement a \"Share\" feature. Generate a summary image or text of a completed workout and allow the user to share it to Instagram, Twitter, or other apps using the native share sheet.','Free marketing! Let users share their workout summaries on social media.',NULL,'Tapping \"Share\" opens the OS share dialog. Selecting \"Messages\" pre-fills the text with \"I just lifted 100kg on Bench Press!\".','Mobile','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(64,4,'Push Notifications','Configure local push notifications. Schedule a notification to remind the user to work out if they haven\'t logged activity for a few days.','Users are forgetting to work out. Nudge them with a friendly push notification.',NULL,'A notification appears on the device simulator after the scheduled time, even if the app is closed.','Mobile','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(65,4,'Dark Mode Support','Implement a dark mode theme. Use the React Native Appearance API to detect the system theme and switch the app\'s colors accordingly.','Everyone loves Dark Mode. Implement it so the app respects the system theme.',NULL,'Toggling the system-wide Dark Mode setting automatically updates the app\'s background to black and text to white.','Frontend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(66,4,'App Store Deployment Prep','Prepare the app for release. Configure the app icon and splash screen. Generate a signed APK (Android) or Archive (iOS) for testing on a physical device.','We are ready to launch. Package the app for the App Store and Google Play.',NULL,'A `.apk` file is generated. Installing it on a phone shows the correct custom app icon.','DevOps','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(67,5,'Database Schema','Design a normalized database schema for a banking system. Create tables for Users, Accounts, and Transfers. Ensure you use appropriate data types (e.g., BIGINT for currency in cents) and foreign key constraints.','You are the lead architect for \"Fortress Bank\". Design a database schema that ensures data integrity for financial records.',NULL,'The PostgreSQL database contains `users`, `accounts`, and `transactions` tables. Foreign keys enforce referential integrity (e.g., a transaction cannot reference a non-existent account).','Database','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(68,5,'Transaction Service','Implement the core money transfer logic using Go. Ensure that transfers are atomic: use database transactions to deduct from one account and credit another. Rollback if any step fails.','Money is disappearing! Implement atomic transactions to ensure that money is never lost during a transfer.',NULL,'Calling the Transfer RPC moves funds between accounts. If the sender has insufficient funds, the transaction fails and no money is deducted.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(69,5,'Security Layer','Implement OAuth2 authentication with JWT. Create middleware to validate tokens on every request. Ensure that users can only access their own accounts (IDOR protection).','We failed the penetration test. Secure the API so users can only access their own data.',NULL,'Requests without a valid Bearer token return a 401 Unauthorized status. Requests with a token for User A cannot access User B\'s account details.','Security','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(70,5,'Containerization','Create a multi-stage Dockerfile for the Go application. Use a minimal base image (like Alpine) for the final stage to reduce the attack surface. Configure the container to run as a non-root user.','The security team wants to minimize the attack surface. Dockerize the app using a minimal base image.',NULL,'Running `docker run banking-api` starts the service. The container image size is under 50MB (using Alpine/Scratch) and runs as a non-root user.','DevOps','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(71,5,'Account Management API','Create REST endpoints for creating new accounts, listing accounts, and viewing account details. Validate all inputs strictly to prevent injection attacks.','We need to onboard new customers. Build the account management API with strict input validation.',NULL,'POST /accounts creates a new account. GET /accounts/{id} returns the account balance. Input validation prevents negative initial balances.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(72,5,'Audit Logging','Implement an immutable audit log. Every time a transaction occurs or a setting is changed, write a record to a separate \"Audit\" table or service. This log should never be deletable.','Compliance requires us to track everything. Implement an immutable audit log for all actions.',NULL,'Every API request results in a new row in the `audit_logs` table, recording the User ID, Action, Timestamp, and IP address.','Security','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(73,5,'Rate Limiting','Implement a Token Bucket or Leaky Bucket algorithm to rate limit API requests. This prevents brute-force attacks and Denial of Service (DoS) attempts.','We are under attack! Implement rate limiting to stop the brute-force attempts.',NULL,'Sending requests faster than the limit (e.g., 10 req/sec) results in a 429 Too Many Requests response.','Security','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(74,5,'Two-Factor Authentication','Add 2FA support using TOTP (Time-based One-Time Password). Generate a QR code for the user to scan with Google Authenticator, and require the code for sensitive actions.','Passwords are not enough. Add 2FA to protect high-value accounts.',NULL,'Scanning the QR code with Google Authenticator adds the account. Entering the generated 6-digit code successfully verifies the user.','Security','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(75,5,'Fraud Detection Rules','Implement a background worker that analyzes transactions. Flag any transaction that exceeds a certain amount or occurs from a suspicious IP address for manual review.','We lost $50k to fraud last week. Implement a system to flag suspicious transactions automatically.',NULL,'A transaction of $10,000 triggers a \"Review Needed\" flag in the database and sends an alert to the admin channel.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(76,5,'Currency Conversion Service','Integrate with an external currency exchange API. Allow users to transfer money between accounts with different currencies, calculating the exchange rate in real-time.','We are going global. Allow users to transfer money between different currencies.',NULL,'Transferring 100 USD to a EUR account credits the correct amount based on the current exchange rate.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(77,5,'API Documentation','Use Swagger/OpenAPI to document your API endpoints. Include details about request parameters, response formats, and error codes. Host the documentation on a public URL.','Partners can\'t figure out how to use our API. Document it properly using Swagger.',NULL,'A Swagger UI page is accessible at `/swagger/index.html`, allowing users to test the API endpoints directly.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(78,5,'Integration Testing','Write integration tests that spin up a test database and run full transaction scenarios. Verify that balances are updated correctly and that invalid transactions are rejected.','We broke the transfer logic again. Write integration tests to prevent regression.',NULL,'Running `go test ./...` executes the integration tests against a Dockerized Postgres instance and passes.','DevOps','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(79,5,'Secret Management','Remove all hardcoded credentials from the code. Use environment variables or a secret management tool (like HashiCorp Vault) to inject database passwords and API keys at runtime.','The intern committed the DB password to GitHub. Move all secrets to environment variables immediately.',NULL,'The codebase contains no passwords. The application fails to start if the `DB_PASSWORD` environment variable is missing.','Security','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(80,5,'Mutual TLS','Configure Mutual TLS (mTLS) for communication between your microservices. This ensures that only authorized services can talk to each other.','Zero Trust is the new standard. Implement mTLS so services verify each other\'s identity.',NULL,'Services communicate over HTTPS with client certificates. A service without a valid certificate is rejected.','Security','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(81,5,'Database Replication','Set up PostgreSQL streaming replication. Configure a primary database for writes and a read replica for read-heavy operations (like viewing transaction history).','The database is the bottleneck. Set up a read replica to offload the read traffic.',NULL,'Data written to the Primary DB appears in the Replica DB within seconds. The application reads from the Replica.','Database','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(82,5,'Kubernetes Deployment','Create Helm charts to deploy your application to a Kubernetes cluster. Define resources (CPU/Memory limits) and configure liveness/readiness probes.','We are moving to the cloud. Package the app as a Helm chart for easy deployment.',NULL,'`helm install banking-app ./charts` deploys the application. Pods restart automatically if they become unresponsive.','DevOps','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(83,5,'Vulnerability Scanning','Integrate a vulnerability scanner (like Trivy or Clair) into your CI pipeline. Fail the build if any high-severity vulnerabilities are found in your dependencies or Docker image.','We can\'t ship vulnerable code. Add a security scan to the CI pipeline.',NULL,'The CI build fails and reports \"CVE-2023-XXXX found in library Y\" if a vulnerable package is used.','Security','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(84,5,'Performance Profiling','Use Go\'s pprof tool to profile your application under load. Identify memory leaks or CPU hotspots and optimize the code accordingly.','The server is using too much RAM. Profile the app to find the memory leak.',NULL,'A flame graph is generated showing CPU usage. The report identifies the most expensive function calls.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(85,6,'Data Collection','Write a Python script to ingest data. You can use the Twitter API (if available) or a public dataset (like the Sentiment140 dataset) from Kaggle. Load the data into a Pandas DataFrame.','We need data to train our model. Scrape or download a dataset of tweets.',NULL,'The script outputs the first 5 rows of the DataFrame (`df.head()`), showing columns for \"text\", \"timestamp\", and \"user\". The data contains at least 1000 rows.','AI/Data','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(86,6,'Sentiment Model','Train a machine learning model (e.g., Logistic Regression or Naive Bayes) to classify text as positive or negative. Use Scikit-learn for vectorization (TF-IDF) and training.','Build a baseline model to classify tweets as positive or negative.',NULL,'The script saves a `model.pkl` file. Running the evaluation function prints an accuracy score > 70% on the test set.','AI/Data','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(87,6,'Advanced NLP','Improve your model using Deep Learning. Implement an LSTM (Long Short-Term Memory) network using PyTorch to capture context and nuance in the text better than the simple classifier.','The baseline model is too simple. Use Deep Learning to capture sarcasm and context.',NULL,'The training loop prints the loss decreasing over epochs. The final model achieves a higher F1-score than the baseline Logistic Regression model.','AI/Data','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(88,6,'Dashboard View','Create a web dashboard using Django. Use Graphene-Django to expose a GraphQL API that allows the frontend to query sentiment data flexibly.','The marketing team needs a dashboard. Build a Django app with a GraphQL API.',NULL,'Visiting `http://localhost:8000/graphql` allows executing a query `{ sentiments { text, score } }` which returns JSON data.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(89,6,'Data Cleaning Pipeline','Build a robust preprocessing pipeline. Remove stop words, URLs, and special characters. Perform lemmatization or stemming to normalize the text before feeding it to the model.','Garbage in, garbage out. Clean the text data to improve model accuracy.',NULL,'Input: \"Check out this link! http://test.com #wow\". Output: \"check link wow\". All text is lowercase and free of special characters.','AI/Data','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(90,6,'Exploratory Data Analysis','Perform EDA to understand your dataset. Create visualizations (histograms of tweet lengths, word clouds of most frequent words) using Matplotlib or Seaborn in a Jupyter Notebook.','Understand the data before modeling. Create some charts to visualize the dataset.',NULL,'The notebook displays a histogram of tweet lengths and a word cloud image. The cells execute without errors.','AI/Data','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(91,6,'Topic Modeling','Use Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA) to identify common topics within the dataset. Group tweets by these topics to see what people are talking about.','What are people talking about? Use unsupervised learning to find common topics.',NULL,'The script prints 5 topics, each with 10 associated keywords (e.g., Topic 1: \"game, play, win, team\").','AI/Data','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(92,6,'Real-time Twitter Stream','Connect to a live data stream (e.g., Twitter Streaming API). Process incoming tweets in real-time, predict their sentiment, and update the database.','We need real-time insights. Connect to the live Twitter stream.',NULL,'The database row count increases in real-time as the script runs. The console logs \"Processed tweet: [Positive]\".','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(93,6,'API for Sentiment Analysis','Expose your trained model via a REST API using Django REST Framework. Allow external applications to send text and receive a sentiment score.','Other apps want to use our model. Expose it as a REST API.',NULL,'POST /api/analyze with body `{\"text\": \"I love this!\"}` returns `{\"sentiment\": \"positive\", \"score\": 0.9}`.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(94,6,'User Authentication','Secure the dashboard so only authorized analysts can view the reports. Implement Django\'s built-in authentication system with login and logout pages.','The dashboard is public! Secure it so only our analysts can see it.',NULL,'Accessing `/dashboard` redirects to `/login`. Logging in with valid credentials grants access.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(95,6,'Export Reports','Add functionality to generate PDF reports of the sentiment analysis. Include charts and summary statistics in the generated document.','Management loves PDFs. Add a button to export the analysis as a report.',NULL,'Clicking \"Export PDF\" downloads a file named `report.pdf` containing the generated charts and tables.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(96,6,'Model Deployment','Package your Django application and the trained model into a Docker container. Ensure the container can be run on any machine with Docker installed.','Deploy the app to the cloud. Dockerize it first.',NULL,'`docker build -t sentiment-app .` completes successfully. The container runs and serves the app.','DevOps','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(97,7,'Frontend Manager','Create a React application that mimics a file explorer. Users should be able to navigate folders, view file lists, and see file details (size, type, date modified).','You are building \"CloudBox\". Start by creating a file explorer UI that feels like a native desktop app.',NULL,'The UI displays a list of files and folders. Clicking a folder navigates into it. The file list shows icons based on file type (e.g., PDF icon for .pdf).','Frontend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(98,7,'S3 Integration','Implement secure file uploads to AWS S3. Create a backend endpoint that generates a pre-signed URL, allowing the frontend to upload files directly to S3 without passing through your server.','We need to store files cheaply and reliably. Integrate AWS S3 for file storage.',NULL,'The backend returns a signed S3 URL. The frontend successfully PUTs the file to that URL, and the file appears in the S3 bucket console.','DevOps','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(99,7,'File Metadata Service','Build a microservice to store file metadata (name, S3 key, owner, parent folder) in MongoDB. This service will be the source of truth for the file structure.','S3 is just a flat object store. We need a database to manage the folder hierarchy and file names.',NULL,'Uploading a file creates a document in the MongoDB `files` collection with `name`, `size`, `s3_key`, and `mime_type` fields.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(100,7,'User Authentication','Implement authentication to ensure users can only access their own files. Use JWTs and middleware to protect your API endpoints.','Users are seeing each other\'s files! Implement strict authentication and authorization.',NULL,'Accessing `/api/files` without a token returns 401. With a token, it returns only the files belonging to the authenticated user.','Security','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(101,7,'Folder Structure Support','Implement logic to handle nested folders. Update your database schema to support a tree structure (e.g., using parent_id references) and create API endpoints to create and delete folders.','Users want to organize their files. Add support for nested folders.',NULL,'The API returns a nested JSON structure or a flat list with `parent_id`. The frontend correctly renders the breadcrumb navigation (e.g., Home > Documents > Work).','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(102,7,'File Sharing','Allow users to share files with others. Generate a unique, time-limited public link that allows anyone with the link to download the file.','I want to send a file to a client. Implement a \"Share Link\" feature.',NULL,'Clicking \"Share\" generates a link like `/share/xyz123`. Opening this link in an incognito window downloads the file. The link expires after 1 hour.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(103,7,'Image Thumbnail Generation','Use AWS Lambda to automatically generate thumbnails for uploaded images. Trigger the Lambda function on S3 object creation events.','Loading full-size images in the list view is too slow. Generate thumbnails automatically.',NULL,'Uploading `image.jpg` to S3 triggers the Lambda, which creates `image_thumb.jpg` in a separate bucket or folder.','DevOps','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(104,7,'File Versioning','Enable S3 versioning and update your application to handle multiple versions of the same file. Allow users to restore previous versions.','I accidentally overwrote an important doc! Implement file versioning so users can restore old files.',NULL,'Uploading a file with the same name creates a new version. The UI shows a \"History\" tab listing previous versions with \"Restore\" buttons.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(105,7,'Drag and Drop Uploads','Enhance the frontend to support drag-and-drop uploads. Show a progress bar for each file being uploaded.','Clicking \"Upload\" is tedious. Add drag-and-drop support.',NULL,'Dragging a file onto the browser window highlights the drop zone. Releasing it starts the upload with a visible progress percentage.','Frontend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(106,7,'Storage Quota Management','Track storage usage per user. Prevent uploads if the user has exceeded their allocated storage quota.','Storage costs are rising. Limit free users to 100MB of storage.',NULL,'If a user has 99MB used of 100MB quota, uploading a 2MB file fails with a \"Quota Exceeded\" error.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(107,7,'Trash Bin','Implement a \"soft delete\" feature. When a file is deleted, move it to a \"Trash\" folder instead of permanently deleting it. Allow users to restore files from the trash.','Users are deleting files by mistake. Add a \"Trash\" bin so they can recover them.',NULL,'Deleted files disappear from the main view but appear in the \"Trash\" view. They can be restored or permanently deleted.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(108,7,'Search Files','Implement a search bar that allows users to find files by name. Index the file metadata in MongoDB or Elasticsearch for fast retrieval.','I have too many files. Add a search bar to find things quickly.',NULL,'Typing \"invoice\" in the search bar instantly filters the file list to show only files containing \"invoice\" in the name.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(109,7,'File Preview','Add a preview feature for common file types (PDF, Images, Text). Use a library like react-pdf or simply an iframe for supported types.','Downloading files to check them is annoying. Add a preview modal.',NULL,'Clicking a PDF file opens a modal displaying the PDF content without downloading it.','Frontend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(110,7,'Multipart Uploads','Support uploading large files (e.g., >100MB) using S3 Multipart Uploads. This improves reliability and allows for pausing/resuming uploads.','Uploading large videos fails often. Implement multipart uploads for better reliability.',NULL,'Uploading a 500MB file works reliably. The network tab shows multiple concurrent PUT requests for different parts of the file.','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(111,7,'CDN Integration','Configure AWS CloudFront to serve your files. This reduces latency for users around the world.','Users in Asia are complaining about slow downloads. Use a CDN to speed things up.',NULL,'File download URLs point to the CloudFront domain (e.g., `d123.cloudfront.net`) instead of the raw S3 bucket URL.','DevOps','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(112,7,'Data Encryption','Ensure all files are encrypted at rest in S3 using Server-Side Encryption (SSE-S3 or SSE-KMS).','Security policy requires encryption at rest. Enable S3 server-side encryption.',NULL,'Inspecting the S3 object properties in the AWS Console shows \"Server-side encryption: Enabled\".','Security','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(113,7,'Access Control Lists','Implement granular permissions (Read, Write, Admin) for shared folders. Allow users to invite others with specific access levels.','I want to share a folder but only for viewing. Implement granular permissions.',NULL,'User A shares a folder with User B (Read Only). User B can view files but cannot upload or delete them.','Security','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(114,7,'Activity Log','Log all file access and modification events. Show users a history of who accessed their files and when.','Who deleted my file? Add an activity log so users can see what happened.',NULL,'The \"Activity\" tab shows a list: \"User A uploaded file.txt\", \"User B downloaded file.txt\".','Backend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(115,8,'Configurator UI','Controls for customization.',NULL,NULL,'Floating UI panel styled with CSS.','Frontend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(116,8,'3D Scene Setup','Initialize the 3D environment.',NULL,NULL,'Canvas rendering a 3D model using Three.js (via JS).','Frontend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(117,8,'Asset Optimization','Optimize 3D assets for web.',NULL,NULL,'Webpack config handling model file loading and compression.','Frontend','2025-11-28 06:30:42','2025-11-28 06:30:42'),(118,8,'Camera Controls','Allow user to rotate view.',NULL,NULL,'Or